### PK - Oxford - May 2026

# Splitting function data based on Deuss et al. (GJI, 2013) and Koelemeijer et al. (GRL, 2013),
# as well as a subset of these that were used to construct SP12RTS.
# The files data_list_arwen-paula and data_list_SP12RTS give lists of all the modes contained in these datasets

# Splitting function coefficients are given for each mode in a separate file ($mode.new).
# These are organised in the following way:

smax 
s t cst cst_err
s t cst cst_err
s t cst cst_err
s t cst cst_err

with:
- smax:      the maximum spherical harmonic degree that has been measured
- s:         the degree of the spherical harmonic degree (from 0 to smax)
- t:         the order of the spherical harmonic degree (from 0 to 2*smax
- cst:       the splitting function coefficient (in raw format)
- cst_err:   the uncertainty in the splitting function coefficient (in raw format)
